ARM64 port (roadmap step 14) — step by step
============================================

Portable code stays in kernel/, mm/, fs/. This directory is CPU-specific only.

Done:
  - Hello on PL011 (QEMU virt)
  - Embedded virt.dtb, FDT /memory + host unit test
  - EL1 vector table + sync fault print
  - PMM bitmap (2 GiB frame index space)
  - EL1 MMU: TTBR0 identity, L0→L1→L2 4K, user alias for ET_EXEC @ 0x400000
  - GICv2 + architected timer
  - Slab kheap + kprintf
  - EL0 + SVC; write + uaccess
  - newc initramfs, BusyBox echo/cat, ash, fork/exec/wait/pipes
  - Alpine aarch64 bash (dynamic musl + readline) as the login shell
  - `make ARCH=arm64 test` greps `bash from MyOS` and `bash-5.2`
  - `make ARCH=arm64 utm-arm64` — native UTM virt VM (serial terminal)

Next (14b rest / 14c):
  - Real VFS + writable files; job control; signals that actually deliver
  - Raspberry Pi bare metal (14c)

Apple Silicon (step 15): see arch/aarch64/apple/PORT (15a doc + DTB probe done).
